# ShedOS ISO package list
#
# Almost everything installs transitively via shedos-meta's depends=(), which
# is auto-generated from packages/official/*.txt + packages/aur.txt +
# shedos-* by scripts/render-meta-depends.sh. Only live-boot essentials are
# listed explicitly here as a belt-and-braces guard against accidental edits
# to base.txt breaking the ISO.

base
linux
linux-firmware
mkinitcpio-archiso

# Bootloader + live-boot extras — required by mkarchiso's strict profile
# validation against bootmodes=('bios.syslinux' 'uefi.grub') in profiledef.sh.
# These resolve transitively through shedos-meta too, but mkarchiso checks
# the literal packages.x86_64 file before resolving dependencies, so they
# must appear explicitly here or the build aborts before squashfs.
syslinux
grub
memtest86+
memtest86+-efi
edk2-shell

# Pin every virtual-dep provider we've chosen. Before the packages.x86_64
# collapse (shedos-meta-only layout), every provider was explicit at root
# level, so pacstrap's DFS resolver picked ours by position. Now that our
# providers are transitive via shedos-meta's depends=(), pacman hits
# `depends=('<virtual>')` from some other package FIRST, auto-picks the
# alphabetical default (which is not always what we want), and conflicts
# with our provider when it's finally pulled in. Listing them explicitly
# here puts them back at the root of the resolution graph.
#
# See each pin for the conflict it prevents:
pipewire-jack              # vs jack2 (default) — from audacity/virtualbox `jack` dep
virtualbox-host-modules-arch  # vs virtualbox-host-dkms (default) — from VIRTUALBOX-HOST-MODULES
qt6-multimedia-ffmpeg      # vs qt6-multimedia-gstreamer — matches default, eliminates prompt

shedos-meta
